[out] I've added `GET /appearance` and `PUT /appearance` and committed them to the current branch. `go vet` is clean and the full `go test ./...` run passes. I did not run `/code-review`, so the change has had no separate review pass.

- **Table:** the new `appearances` table is created with `CREATE TABLE IF NOT EXISTS` in `InitDB` (`models/user.go`). Existing databases gain it on startup without losing data. `models/appearance.go` holds the get and upsert helpers.
- **`GET`:** returns the saved document, or 404 if none is saved.
- **`PUT`:** replaces the whole document. It returns 400 and saves nothing if a value isn't `#rrggbb` or a key isn't `head`, `body` or `eyes`. The request body is capped at 4 KB.
- **Auth:** both endpoints return 401 without a valid token.
- **Tests:** `handlers/appearance_test.go` covers every acceptance criterion. That includes the table being re-created on a database that lacks it, and a failed `PUT` leaving an existing document unchanged.

The issue doesn't say whether all three keys are required, so I let a `PUT` omit any of them (an empty `{}` is accepted). Say if you want all three enforced.

The app was not restarted. Run PM2 manually to deploy, since the new route is in `main.go`. The untracked `logs/` directory was already there and I left it out of the commit.

